Every certificate authority in this directory can issue a certificate for ANY
domain that vrl will believe. That is what a trust store is.

A normal distro ships ~150 of these. vrl ships the ones it needs and no
more, and because they live in git, adding one is a visible commit with a
diff -- not an invisible default.

  isrg-root-x1.pem   Let's Encrypt / ISRG Root X1.
                     sha256 96:BC:EC:06:...:DF:08:C6
                     Verified two ways: fetched from letsencrypt.org AND
                     byte-compared against heatpc's system trust store.
                     Needed because irc.libera.chat chains to it.

`./build.sh ta` compiles these into ta.h, which is linked into tlstunnel. The
anchors end up inside the signed, verity-covered image -- nobody can drop an
extra CA into a directory at runtime.
